 EXTENDED COMMAND SUMMARY
  (note periods: ".")

 **** These commands are for AIDES only
   .<A>ide ?
   .<A>ide <A>dd-file
   .<A>ide <C>hat
   .<A>ide <D>elete-empty-rooms
   .<A>ide <E>dit-room
   .<A>ide <I>nsert-pulled-message
   .<A>ide <K>ill-room

 **** These commands are for everyone else
   .<E>nter ?

   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <A>ddress <forwarding on the net>
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <B>iography <for use with <M>eet User>
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <C>omplete-reconfigure
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <E>xpert
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <F>loor-mode
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <H>alf-duplex
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <L>inefeeds
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <M>ail-Forwarding
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <N>ulls
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <O>ld on New toggle
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <P>rompt
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <T>ime of Messages
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <W>idth of Screen
   .<E>nter <C>onfiguration <Z>Old-RE

   .<E>nter <F>ile                          (via XMODEM)
   .<E>nter <X>modem <F>ile
   .<E>nter <Y>modem <F>ile
   .<E>nter <W>xmodem <F>ile
   .<E>nter <M>essage
   .<E>nter <X>modem <M>essage
   .<E>nter <Y>modem <M>essage
   .<E>nter <W>xmodem <M>essage
   .<E>nter <N>et-Message   (People with net privileges ONLY)
   .<E>nter <X>modem <N>et-Message            "
   .<E>nter <Y>modem <N>et-message            "
   .<E>nter <W>xmodem <N>et-message           "
                     (Also see .Help PROTOCOL)
   .<E>nter <P>assword
   .<E>nter <R>oom
   .<E>nter <H>eld-Message

   .<G>oto ?
   .<G>oto ANYROOM
   .<G>oto PARTIALROOMNAME

   .<H>elp ?
   .<H>elp ANYFILE

   .<K>nown ?
   .<K>nown <A>nonymous-rooms
   .<K>nown <D>irectory-rooms
   .<K>nown <I>nformation          <display information of all known rooms>
   .<K>nown <M>atch match-string   <search room list for matching room name>
   .<K>nown <P>rivate-rooms
   .<K>nown <R>ead-only rooms
   .<K>nown <S>hared-rooms
   .<K>nown <Z>Forgotten-rooms

   .<L>ogin PASSWORD

   .<M>eet User <username>
   .<M>eet User ?     <list of users with biographies>

   .<R>ead ?
   .<R>ead <F>orward [date-spec]    <a date-spec is: yymmmdd>
   .<R>ead <N>ew [date-spec]
   .<R>ead <O>ld-Reverse [date-spec]
   .<R>ead <R>everse [date-spec]

      < These may be used in combination with each other and the above>
   .<R>ead <L>ocal-only <any option> <reads local messages only in shared rooms>
   .<R>ead <U>ser ...                <reads messages from specified users>
   .<R>ead <P>hrase ...              <search for specified phrase in msgs>
   .<R>ead <G>lobal ...              <read all rooms using Phrase, New, etc... >

   .<R>ead <C>ompressed ...          <compress messages -- not all installations>

        (NFOR == New, Forward, Reverse, Old)
   .<R>ead <X>modem [NFOR]                    <CRC supported>
   .<R>ead <Y>modem [NFOR]                    <YMODEM SINGLE only>
   .<R>ead <W>xmodem [NFOR]
                     (Also see .Help PROTOCOL)

   .<R>ead <I>nvited        (Sysop only)
   .<R>ead <S>tatus

   .<R>ead <D>irectory              <This group apply only to directory rooms.>
   .<R>ead <D>irectory *.DOC [date-spec]
   .<R>ead <E>xtended-directory
   .<R>ead <E>xtended-directory *.DOC [date-spec]
   .<R>ead <G>lobal <D>irectory ...
   .<R>ead <G>lobal <E>xtended-directory ...
   .<R>ead <B>inaryfile
   .<R>ead <T>extfile <C/R>
   .<R>ead <T>extfile <F>ormatted
   .<R>ead <X>modem <B>inaryFile               <CRC supported>
   .<R>ead <X>modem <T>extfile                 <CRC supported>
   .<R>ead <Y>modem [T|B]                    <YMODEM BATCH only>
   .<R>ead <P>hrase <directory command>     <searches file comments for phrase>
                                        <see FILES.HLP.>

   .<R>ead <A>rchive <D>irectory      <Reads compressed file Table of Contents>
                                <ARC, ZIP, ZOO, LZH files supported>

         < These 4 commands may not be available >
   .<R>ead <A>rchive <B>inary-files   <Reads files FROM the arc for download>
   .<R>ead <X>modem <A>rchive <B>inary-files    <May also use 'T' or 'F' as synonyms>
   .<R>ead <Y>modem <A>rchive <B>inary-files
                     (Also see .Help PROTOCOL)

   .<S>kip ?
   .<S>kip ANYROOM
   .<S>kip PARTIALROOMNAME

   .<T>erminate ?
   .<T>erminate <A>bort
   .<T>erminate <S>tay
   .<T>erminate <Q>uit-also

   .<U>ngoto ANYROOM
   .<U>ngoto PARTIALROOMNAME

   .<Z>     <Lists public forgotten rooms>

 FLOOR COMMANDS

 **** These commands are for AIDES only
   ;<A>ide <C>reate-floor
   ;<A>ide <D>elete empty floors
   ;<A>ide <F>loor <M>oderator
   ;<A>ide <K>ill-floor
   ;<A>ide <M>ove rooms
   ;<A>ide <R>ename-floor

 **** These commands are for everyone else
   ;<C>onfigure switch (from Floor mode to Normal mode)
   ;<G>oto FLOORNAME
   ;<K>nown floors
   ;<S>kip FLOORNAME
   ;<Z>    Forgets current Floor


 %ADVANCED Back to the advanced commands help menu.
 %HELPOPT Get a list of all help files in the system.
 %MAINHELP First level of help system.

